@bio:

Kateryna Schöning, PD Dr, studied and completed her PhD in
Kharkiv (Ukraine), worked 2008-2016 in Leipzig, Mannheim,
and since 2016 in Vienna, where she carried out numerous
research projects on music before and around 1600. She is
currently a Senior Scientist at the Department of
Musicology at the University of Vienna and head of the
E-LAUTE project (www.e-laute.info). She mainly focuses on
the interdisciplinary research on the music in the 16th
century, i.a. the relationships between music and humanism,
music and texts, as well as the topics of digital
humanities and music editing. 2024 she finished her second
book Loci Communes and Tablatures in the German Area in the
16th Century (Hollitzer, 2025) -
https://www.jstor.org/content/oa_book_monograph/jj.34829427.
More: www.katerynaschoening.at



@@END: BIO